### Exception Hierarchy
- Java exception hierarchy starts from Object → Throwable → Error / Exception, where exceptions are divided into checked and unchecked.
- Throwable class acess root for java Exception Hierarchy.
- it contains two child class. 1. exception 2 error

Java Exception Hierarchy (Full Diagram)
Object
 │
 └── Throwable
     │
     ├── Error
     │   │
     │   ├── VirtualMachineError
     │   │   ├── OutOfMemoryError
     │   │   └── StackOverflowError
     │   │
     │   ├── AssertionError
     │   └── LinkageError
     │       └── NoClassDefFoundError
     │
     └── Exception
         │
         ├── IOException
         │   ├── FileNotFoundException
         │   └── EOFException
         │
         ├── SQLException
         │
         ├── ClassNotFoundException
         │
         ├── InterruptedException
         │
         └── RuntimeException   (Unchecked)
             │
             ├── ArithmeticException
             ├── NullPointerException
             ├── ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
             ├── StringIndexOutOfBoundsException
             ├── NumberFormatException
             └── ClassCastException

Note:-
- Throwable → root of all exceptions and errors
- Error → system/JVM issues (not recoverable)
- Exception → application-level problems
- Checked Exceptions → handled at compile time
- Unchecked Exceptions → runtime errors (RuntimeException)
